#ETH With liquidity returning, ETH’s volatility is also starting to increase. Before major macro developments land, it may not be able to break through as quickly as last week.
The extreme support below is not the weekend low at 2460, but around 2430 near the midpoint of the entire range; conditions are relatively bullish above the midline;

Alternatively, you can treat the short-term range as fluctuations between 2430 and 2550. Since the lower horizontal support is farther away, it’s better to wait for a pullback opportunity around the upper end at 2550/2570. ​​​

#美联储加息 

Starting this week, central banks around the world will convene a series of interest-rate meeting sessions, releasing new rate decision announcements;

The market is set to experience violent fluctuations, with both risks and opportunities coexisting;

Mingyi does not discuss whether there will be a rate hike—truly resilient trading systems don’t need to look at short-term fundamental changes to prove themselves;

The viewpoint remains unchanged—reiterating once again:

1: The probability of seeing ETH below 1505 within the year is very low

2: BTC 57800 is not the year’s low

“Within the year” means before December 31, 2026 (Gregorian calendar)

